        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-1.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cyl. <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cyl. Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">euua. <hi rend="italic">R T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">euua. R T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der historische Satz, aus <hi rend="italic">A. apost.</hi> 11, 22. 15, 22 verwirrt, von Q vereinfacht, will nur den Brief El 49, 3 einführen und damit zum christlichen Recht überleiten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The historical sentence, garbled from <hi rend="italic">A. apost.</hi> 11, 22. 15, 22 and simplified by Q, is meant only to introduce the letter El 49, 3 and thereby to lead over to Christian law</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H corr modernisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H corr modernises</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘und Cilicien’ Q aus Vulg. oder El 49, 2. Ebenso Lambarde unter <hi rend="italic">Errata</hi> ‘interpone <hi rend="italic">⁊ to Cilicia</hi>’ schwerlich nur aus Br übersetzend, sondern gemäss verlorener Agsä. Vorlage</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘and Cilicia’ Q from Vulg. or El 49, 2. Likewise Lambarde under <hi rend="italic">Errata</hi> ‘interpone <hi rend="italic">⁊ to Cilicia</hi>’, hardly merely translating from Br, but following a lost Anglo-Saxon exemplar</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
